{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SbnhFRvMXKMzGMjYboNMtB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs. Re-implementations built from docs alone diverge on edge cases. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility Go implementations, `pkg/` holds shared libraries (sys, format, testutils), `magefiles/` provides build targets, and `docs/` holds human-authored specifications (PRDs, use cases, test suites).\n\n**Current state**: Specs are complete for testutils, sys, format, ts, wc, cat, sponge, du, and ls. Generated code exists at `generation-merged` tags but NOT on the working branch. All code statuses show \"not started\" on the current branch.\n\n**Current release**: Release 03.0 — \"Batch 3 — wc specification and differential test.\" Use case `rel03.0-uc001-wc` has spec_complete status with code not started.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 03.0 has one use case: `rel03.0-uc001-wc`. The spec (PRD, use case, test suite) is complete, so the next step is code generation. Per P2, implementation and tests must be separate tasks. With a limit of 1 task, I propose the implementation task. The wc utility depends only on Go standard library — no pkg/ dependencies needed — so it has no code prerequisites.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/wc core counting (-l, -w, -c) -- rel03.0-uc001-wc\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (glob for prd*-wc.yaml to find the wc PRD)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel03.0-uc001-wc.yaml (wc use case -- end-to-end execution path)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-03.0.yaml (wc test suite -- expected inputs and outputs)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ component conventions and project structure)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/wc/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"wc utility -- flag parsing, counting logic for lines/words/bytes, file and stdin input, formatted output, exit codes\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement line counting (-l), word counting (-w), and byte counting (-c) per the wc PRD counting requirements\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"When no counting flags are specified, default output shows three columns: lines, words, bytes\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Read input from named file arguments; when no file arguments are given, read from stdin\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"When multiple files are given, print per-file counts and a final totals line labeled 'total'\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Exit 0 on success; exit 1 when any named file cannot be opened; print the error to stderr and continue processing remaining files\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Single main.go in cmd/wc/ per project convention of one package per utility\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use Go standard library only -- os, bufio, fmt, flag, io; no pkg/ dependencies needed for wc\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Right-justify numeric columns to match GNU wc field-width behavior -- minimum column width derived from the largest count across all files\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"'go build ./cmd/wc/' compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Binary counts lines, words, and bytes correctly for a single file\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Binary reads from stdin when invoked with no file arguments\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Multiple file arguments produce per-file counts followed by a 'total' line\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Default output (no flags) shows lines, words, bytes in three right-justified columns\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"Nonexistent file produces an error on stderr, exit code 1, and does not prevent processing of remaining files\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21103,"cache_read_input_tokens":14011,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":21103,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99c06913-6b87-49c1-9229-68b2f8cc953d","uuid":"b43bd23e-6783-424a-a70a-3162cfba0047"}
